 "result_text": "`bytes_sql_quote()` in `src/DocumentTemplate/DT_Var.py` now returns text on Python 3, so `<dtml-sqlvar xy type=\"string\">` output can be concatenated with the rest of the query. I haven't run the tests or tried it on a real query.\n\nAfter removing and doubling the dangerous characters, the function decodes the result as UTF-8, as in the patch from the issue. I guarded the decode with `six.PY3`. On Python 2, `bytes` is `str`, and decoding would turn it into `unicode`, so it still returns the plain string there.\n\nBytes that aren't valid UTF-8 will now raise a `UnicodeDecodeError` instead of passing through.\n\nThe system reported that `DT_Var.py` changed on disk after my edit. I didn't look at what changed, so I haven't checked that my edit is still in place.",
